From bda9d0f74f97c670e11d5a887188b3a720265d08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 11:07:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 082/206] feat(shorebird): the object pool mapper, and what the
 385 indices are for

Disassembling InitializeWithObjectPoolLinkInfo finishes the three-stage mapper
and settles a question this tree had explicitly recorded as open.

The object pool link info's trailing index list -- 385 entries, carried under a
descriptive name because three hypotheses about it had been tested and refuted
-- is the mapper's pair-constraint list. Their code reads that very vector at
0x10019d7c0 and loads mapping[i] together with mapping[i + 1] at 0x10019d7cc.
Each index asserts the two pool slots stay adjacent, so a known side fixes the
unknown one: forwards at 0x10019d7f0, backwards at 0x10019d80c. Skipped when
both are known and when neither is. 292 of the 385 had exactly one side mapped
after stage 1, which is the number their report prints.

So the field is renamed from indices_ to pair_constraints_ and retyped to
int32_t, which is what their `ldrsw ... lsl #2` indexes it as.

Two more details that were not guessable:

Stage 1 skips a pair unless both indices are at least 8 (cmp/ccmp at
0x10019d72c). The pool's first eight slots are fixed.

Backfill is not simply "lowest free". When both halves of a constraint are
still unmapped it searches for the first index whose successor is also free,
takes both, advances the loop an extra step and counts two (w21 = 2 at
0x10019da68). A lowest-free search would break the pair.

One test failed on the first run and it was the test that was wrong: it paired
base index 1, which stage 1's own floor discards, so the slot backfilled
instead. Rewritten to exercise what it claims -- two claimed bases leaving 8
and 10 free but neither with a free successor, so the pair has to land at 12.

Negative control: flipping the backward derivation from b - 1 to b + 1 turns
the derivation test red and leaves the other four green, which is right, since
those four do not exercise that direction.

113 tests pass; verify_all.sh reports 5 ran, 0 failed, 0 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
index a067b97aae9..d7da72eb668 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.cc
@@ -450,15 +450,23 @@ std::unique_ptr<ObjectPoolLinkInfo> ObjectPoolLinkInfo::ReadFromStream(
     codes.push_back(std::move(info));
   }
 
-  std::vector<uintptr_t> indices;
-  if (!ReadIndexVector(stream, &indices)) return nullptr;
+  // Their element type is int32_t (the mapper indexes this with
+  // `ldrsw ... lsl #2`), but the wire form is the same unsigned varint list.
+  std::vector<uintptr_t> raw;
+  if (!ReadIndexVector(stream, &raw)) return nullptr;
+  std::vector<int32_t> pair_constraints;
+  pair_constraints.reserve(raw.size());
+  for (uintptr_t v : raw) {
+    if (v > static_cast<uintptr_t>(kMaxInt32)) return nullptr;
+    pair_constraints.push_back(static_cast<int32_t>(v));
+  }
 
   if (stream->PendingBytes() <= 0) return nullptr;
   const intptr_t num_pool_entries = stream->ReadUnsigned<intptr_t>();
   if (num_pool_entries < 0) return nullptr;
 
   return std::unique_ptr<ObjectPoolLinkInfo>(new ObjectPoolLinkInfo(
-      std::move(codes), std::move(indices), num_pool_entries));
+      std::move(codes), std::move(pair_constraints), num_pool_entries));
 }
 
 void ObjectPoolLinkInfo::WriteToStream(BaseWriteStream* stream) const {
@@ -469,7 +477,11 @@ void ObjectPoolLinkInfo::WriteToStream(BaseWriteStream* stream) const {
     WriteIndexVector(stream, info.self_pp_indices_);
     WriteIndexVector(stream, info.subgraph_pp_indices_);
   }
-  WriteIndexVector(stream, indices_);
+  stream->WriteUnsigned<intptr_t>(
+      static_cast<intptr_t>(pair_constraints_.size()));
+  for (int32_t v : pair_constraints_) {
+    stream->WriteUnsigned<intptr_t>(static_cast<intptr_t>(v));
+  }
   // Trailing, like the class and field tables' sizes.
   stream->WriteUnsigned<intptr_t>(num_pool_entries_);
 }
diff --git a/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.h b/runtime/vm/shorebird/link_info.h
